# <type>: <imperative summary, <=72 chars>
#
# Types: feat | fix | docs | design | test | refactor | chore | build
#   feat     - new user-facing behavior
#   fix      - bug fix
#   docs     - README/docs/*.md changes only
#   design   - docs/design.md, docs/requirements.md, docs/system-design/*
#              changes that alter or extend the design itself (not just
#              wording), kept distinct from "docs" so design-shape changes
#              are easy to find in history
#   test     - test-only changes (no behavior change)
#   refactor - code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   chore    - tooling, CI, dependency bumps
#   build    - packaging (pyproject.toml, requirements.txt)
#
# Why this change? (one or two sentences — the "what" is in the diff, this
# is for the "why". Reference the FR/NFR or docs/plan.md phase if relevant.)

# What was tested? (brief — full detail belongs in the PR description, but
# a one-liner here helps `git log`/`git blame` readers later.)

# Related issue/PR, if any:
